{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>Two sockets under the one board.</b> The sockets — their length is one cubit, like the thickness of the board, and their width is three quarters of a cubit, which is half the length of the board. The length of the socket is set along the thickness of the board and its width along the width of the board. And each socket, in its middle, has a hollowed-out hole a quarter cubit by a quarter cubit. It turns out that from the edge of the hole to the edge of the socket is half a cubit less half a quarter on this side, and half a cubit less half a quarter on that side, and from the edge of the hole to the edge of the length is a quarter cubit on this side and a quarter cubit on that side. The board is grooved across its width a quarter cubit on this side and a quarter cubit on that side, and in its middle a groove half a cubit; and further the board is grooved across its thickness half a cubit less half a quarter on this side, and half a cubit less half a quarter on that side. Another wording: a quarter cubit and a half on this side, and a quarter cubit and a half on that side — and it is all one; the tenon that remains is a quarter cubit thick. It turns out that the tenons of each and every board, each one, are a quarter cubit by a quarter cubit. And when he would insert the tenons into the holes of the sockets, the thickness of the grooves would cover the edges of the sockets on every side precisely."], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:00:39.442225411Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}